'' is not a fleet verb. The 30 verbs are: abort, apply, base-check, board, brief, close, compaction-status, complete, declare, dispatch, enroll, harvest, init, leases, lint, milestone, pane-guard, park, propose, reap, reconcile, resume, review, roadmap, selftest, set-golden, status, unenroll, unpark, verify.
fleet <verb> [flags]                          v0.1.0

verbs:
    abort                abandon an inflight instant: rename it -abort- WITH A RECORDED REASON (FD-12)
    apply                the COORDINATOR applies a proposal; the single writer
    base-check           is this workspace positioned on the base its milestone builds on? (SI-19/SI-32)
    board                every subject HOLDING A SLOT, and nothing else (FD-4)
    brief                what a dispatched instant needs to know about itself: coordinator, milestone, phase, gate, where its next report will land, and what is outstanding
    close                shut a pane this store owns and stamp the record; disarms the monitor (FD-10)
    compaction-status    whether a compaction is holding every dispatch
    complete             pass the gate, then rename the folder -complete-
    declare              declare a phase and print what the CONSUMER now reads
    dispatch             evaluate every gate, then dispatch one worker
    enroll               put an EXISTING workspace directory into the pool; opt-in
    harvest              the harvest transaction, plus the observation tick
    init                 bootstrap a new instant from the layout matrix
    leases               every enrolled slot and who holds it
    lint                 the layout matrix, the watched-source registry, the near-miss rule
    milestone            the COORDINATOR puts a milestone ON the roadmap; the only way work becomes dispatchable
    pane-guard           the send-keys contract: 0 safe / 10 queued / 11 mid-turn / 12 not-claude / 13 unknown
    park                 record a parked decision as structured state
    propose              the WORKER's status proposal; never a roadmap write
    reap                 free every stale lease this base OWNS; name the ones it does not
    reconcile            the ARM SET the external monitor reads, from the one join (FD-10); read-only
    resume               adopt an existing conforming instant; NO admission rule (FD-9)
    review               record a structured round and report the gate
    roadmap              milestones, readiness, blockers and pending proposals
    selftest             discover and run every suite; the tree state is ALWAYS stamped (AC-10)
    set-golden           declare the golden workspace; there is deliberately no fallback (MI-7)
    status               one subject in full, with the evidence behind its state
    unenroll             take a slot out of the pool
    unpark               clear a parked decision
    verify               EXECUTE every documented recipe in a sandbox (F-14)

fleet abort --instant <value> --reason <value>
    abandon an inflight instant: rename it -abort- WITH A RECORDED REASON (FD-12)
    --instant <value>            (required) the instant to abandon
    --reason <value>             (required) why the work stopped; mandatory and recorded — an abort with no reason is a deletion with a nicer name
    --home <value>               the record/pool store root; overrides $FLEET_HOME
    --instants-dir <value>       where instants live; overrides $FLEET_INSTANTS
    --porcelain                  machine form on stdout: tab-separated, no banner (NFR2-7)
    --help                       print this verb's derived usage and exit 0
    --dry-run                    evaluate every gate and CREATE NOTHING; the delta is asserted to be zero

